:210,"description":"Get tips and tricks for teaching AI-900 Microsoft Azure AI Fundamentals","resourceUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/get-tips-tricks-teach-ai-900-microsoft-azure-ai-fundamentals/?WT.mc_id=api_CatalogApi","sourceType":"provider-catalogue"},{"id":"mslearn-fa7adad3ebf0e5b1","version":"2026-10-21T17:02:00+00:00","title":"Tune queries in Azure Database for PostgreSQL","provider":"Microsoft Learn","category":"Programming","level":"Intermediate","hours":0.52,"skills":["Cloud Computing"],"cost":0,"rating":0,"learners":0,"online":true,"delivery":"online","setting":"indoor","hrdc":false,"instructor":"Microsoft Learn","hue":210,"description":"Relational databases store many different types of data for many different types of applications. Some databases have thousands of users and some have just one user. Some tables have tens of rows while others have millions of rows. Some data is unique while other data is duplicated. All of these variables mean that database management systems (DBMSs) need systems to understand the data and the queries that are running against this data to ensure optimum performance. When you perform tune a database, it's important to understand how performance tuning works and how you can assess performance metrics.","resourceUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/tune-queries-azure-database-for-postgresql/?WT.mc_id=api_CatalogApi","sourceType":"provider-catalogue"},{"id":"mslearn-a0fdf18409d0f908","version":"2026-10-21T17:02:00+00:00","title":"Manage Azure PaaS tasks using automation","provider":"Microsoft Learn","category":"Programming","level":"Intermediate","hours":1.13,"skills":["Cloud Computing"],"cost":0,"rating":0,"learners":0,"online":true,"delivery":"online","setting":"indoor","hrdc":false,"instructor":"Microsoft Learn","hue":210,"description":"Manage Azure PaaS tasks using automation","resourceUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/manage-azure-paas-resources-using-au